From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mpv): log a fresh Dolby success record after each reset

The physical-target success record ("automatic DV physical target ...
generation N") was logged once per render generation. A frame-queue
reset (a seek, a new file or a queue refill) resets the queue and the
provider without changing that generation, so no record followed the
reset. Clients discard their record when the source changes, as
native-dovi-target-state documents, and a player that replaced its
stream mid-title lost its renderer facts for the rest of the play.

Clear the logged flag where the queue and provider are reset. The
record still prints only from a successful private map on the physical
path, so a reset after which mapping stays inactive logs nothing.
---
 DOCS/man/input.rst      | 4 +++-
 video/out/vo_gpu_next.c | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
index 20d87a494..4c6355467 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -3906,7 +3906,9 @@ Property list
     Active eligibility alone does not prove that a picture was Dolby mapped.
     A client reporting successful mapping must also match the generation in
     the renderer's successful mapping record. Source changes require a fresh
-    success record. ``video-target-params`` continues to describe the encoded
+    success record: after any frame-queue reset (a seek, a new file or a
+    queue refill) the renderer logs its record again on its first successful
+    mapping, even when the generation is unchanged. ``video-target-params`` continues to describe the encoded
     video signal and can differ from the physical display target.
 
 ``vo-passes``
diff --git a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
index 1a73d6c92..373f46c79 100644
--- a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,11 @@ static bool draw_frame(struct vo *vo, struct vo_frame *frame)
         if (p->want_reset) {
             pl_queue_reset(p->queue);
             dv_provider387_reset(p->dovi_provider);
+            // A new source, seek position or refill starts mapping afresh. Clients
+            // discard their success record when the source changes, and the
+            // physical-target generation need not change with it, so the
+            // next successful private map logs its record again.
+            p->dovi_physical_logged = false;
             p->last_pts = 0.0;
             p->last_id = 0;
             p->want_reset = false;
